d 'XTASYM': module to analyze directional asymmetry with panel data: partial sums, diagnostics and graphics
d
d   xtasym builds, describes and draws the positive and negative
d partial sums used to test directional asymmetry with panel data:
d whether an increase in a regressor has an effect equal and
d opposite to a decrease. It implements the partial-sum
d decomposition of Shin, Yu and Greenwood-Nimmo (2014) as used by
d Thombs, Huang and Fitzgerald (2022, Sociological Methodology
d 52:1-29), and the cumulated components of Allison (2019, Socius
d 5:1-12), selectable with a convention() option, since the two
d differ in the sign of the negative arm and therefore in the
d symmetry restriction to be tested. Beyond construction, the
d command reports the diagnostics needed to choose an estimator for
d those series: a directional frequency table, the within and
d between dispersion of each partial sum, the Pesaran (2015) CD
d test for cross-sectional dependence (computed internally, so no
d other package is needed), and the Pesaran (2007) CIPS panel
d unit-root test. It also produces three publication-quality
d figures in a choice of four colour ramps, including a
d colour-blind-safe one.  
d
d KW: panel data
d KW: structural breaks
d KW: directional symmetry
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260820
d
d Author:   Merwan Roudane, NA
d Support: email  merwanroudane920@@gmail.com
d
f xtasym.ado
f xtasym.sthlp
f xtasym_methods.sthlp
f xtasym_example.do
